  "body_html": "<h1>Von Neumann Minimax Theorem</h1>\n<p>Every finite two-player zero-sum matrix game has a value in mixed strategies:</p>\n<p>$$\\max_x \\min_j E_A(x,j) = \\min_y \\max_i E_A(i,y).$$</p>\n<p>Equivalently, there are optimal mixed strategies $x^\\ast$ and $y^\\ast$ and a\nvalue $v$ such that player I guarantees at least $v$ against every column and\nplayer II holds player I to at most $v$ against every row.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>The library closes this statement by the simplified-Loomis route\n<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"zero_sum.minimax.minimax_from_loomis\" href=\"minimax/zero_sum_minimax_minimax_from_loomis.html\">Minimax Theorem by Simplified Loomis Induction</a>: strong induction on\n$|I| + |J|$, using simplex compactness and continuity from\n<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"zero_sum.loomis_route_compactness\" href=\"zero_sum_loomis_route_compactness.html\">Compactness and Continuity Scaffold for the Loomis Route</a> and the existence /\nweak-duality scaffold in <a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"zero_sum.lam_mu_existence\" href=\"zero_sum_lam_mu_existence.html\">Existence of Optimal Mixed Strategies (Loomis Foundations)</a>.  The weak\ninequality maximin $\\le$ minimax holds in general\n(<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"zero_sum.maximin_le_minimax\" href=\"zero_sum_maximin_le_minimax.html\">Maximin is Bounded by Minimax</a>); the induction supplies optimal\nstrategies whose guarantees meet at a single value, forcing equality.</p>\n<p>A second, ordered-field-generic route via Dantzig pivots is sketched as a\nseparate proof-plan node (<code>zero_sum.dantzig_proof_spine</code>): its algebraic\nscaffolding is fully proved, but the simplex-termination step at the top of\nthe induction is still open and tracked as a staged proof-plan.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Chapter 2, Thm. 2.3.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Von Neumann minimax theorem for finite zero-sum games.</li>\n</ul>",
